-- title:
--   Relative degree of the level-N function field over k(̃ j_N)
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N \neq 0$ and a field $k$. Inside the field of Laurent series $k((q))$ put $\tilde j =$ `jqModC k`, the series $q^{-1}$ times the image in $k$ of the integral power series `jNum` $= E_4^3 \cdot$ `dedekindEtaUnitInv` (the $q$-expansion of $j$ with coefficients reduced into $k$), and $\tilde j_N =$ `jqNModC k N`, obtained from $\tilde j$ by the substitution $q \mapsto q^N$ (the ring map `qExpand` multiplying all exponents by $N$). Let $C =$ `modularFunctionFieldC k N` be the intermediate field of $k((q))/k$ generated by $\{\tilde j, \tilde j_N\}$. Let `data` be modular polynomial data of level $N$: a polynomial $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$, monic of degree $\psi(N)$ in $Y$ with $\Phi(j(q), j(q^N)) = 0$ in $\mathbb{Q}((q))$, where $\psi(N) = \sum_{d \mid N,\ d \text{ squarefree}} N/d$ is `dedekindPsi N`. Assume `EvalSymm data.Φ`: for all $x, y \in \mathbb{Q}((q))$ one has $\Phi(x, y) = \Phi(y, x)$, where the first argument is substituted into the coefficients via `Polynomial.aeval` and the second into the outer variable. Assume further that the relative finrank of $k(\tilde j)$ in $C$ equals $\psi(N)$. The conclusion is that the relative finrank of $k(\tilde j_N)$ in $C$ also equals $\psi(N)$.
--
--   This is the transfer of the degree computation for the level-$N$ modular function field across the swap of the two generators of the modular correspondence, effected by the symmetry $\Phi(X,Y) = \Phi(Y,X)$ of the modular polynomial; the proof cites the vanishing of $\Phi$ at the pairs $(\tilde j_d, \tilde j_{d\ell})$ and, under the symmetry hypothesis, at $(\tilde j_{d\ell}, \tilde j_d)$. It feeds the squarefree-level degree statement [`ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqNModC_eq_finrank_adjoin_jqModC_of_squarefree`](thm.html#ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqNModC_eq_finrank_adjoin_jqModC_of_squarefree) and the comparison with the Igusa function field of $X_1$ in characteristic $p$.
